=== Validation evidence of each cohort that is independent of this pipeline ===
  'Independent' means that the evidence does not rest on the internal consistency of this pipeline but agrees with external facts.
  GSE111629  sex check 1.0000    DNAm age agrees with recorded age
  GSE112611  sex check 1.0000    DNAm age agrees with recorded age (narrow age range, weaker evidence); higher neutrophils in cases
  GSE144858  sex check 1.0000    DNAm age agrees with recorded age
  GSE145361  sex check 1.0000    agrees with the published summary statistics of Vallerga et al. (rho=0.581)
  GSE198904  sex check not finished  DNAm age agrees with recorded age
  GSE273970  sex check 0.9929    none: age only in ten-year groups, no external comparison so far
  GSE338167  sex check not finished  DNAm age agrees with recorded age
  GSE80417   sex check 1.0000    DNAm age agrees with recorded age; higher smoking score in cases, in line with the literature
  GSE84727   sex check not finished  DNAm age agrees with recorded age; higher smoking score in cases, in line with the literature
  GSE87648   sex check 0.9471    DNAm age agrees with recorded age; higher neutrophils in cases fit inflammatory bowel disease

  Note: agreement of DNAm age with recorded age verifies two things at once - the correspondence between probe names and values
  is correct (the clock takes coefficients by probe; a shift would not give ages), and the correspondence between samples and phenotypes is correct
  (the ages compared come from the records). GSE273970 has no external comparison on either side; the sex check of this step
  is its only independent evidence.

=== GSE273970: does DNAm age agree with the ten-year age groups? ===
  This cohort has no numeric age but ten-year groups, which allow a test of the rank order.
  Distribution of groups: 21-30=49; 31-40=67; 41-50=89; 51-60=56; 61-70=14; 71-80=8
  Spearman correlation between group midpoints and DNAm age = 0.904
    21-30      n= 49  median DNAm age 27.1
    31-40      n= 67  median DNAm age 36.8
    41-50      n= 89  median DNAm age 43.8
    51-60      n= 56  median DNAm age 50.8
    61-70      n= 14  median DNAm age 55.7
    71-80      n=  8  median DNAm age 61.2
  Decision: pass, rank order agrees

